{
  "id": "26939_chiyusuru",
  "headword": "{治癒|ちゆ}する",
  "reading": "ちゆする",
  "romaji": "chiyusuru",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "to heal; to recover; to be cured",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to heal; to recover; to be cured",
      "explanation": "For a disease, injury, or condition to be fully healed or cured. A formal, medical term indicating complete recovery."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "26939_chiyusuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{傷|きず}が{完全|かんぜん}に{治癒|ちゆ}した。",
      "english": "The wound healed completely.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26939_chiyusuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{自然|しぜん}{治癒|ちゆ}{力|りょく}を{高|たか}めることが{大切|たいせつ}だ。",
      "english": "It is important to strengthen the body's natural healing power.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26939_chiyusuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "この{病気|びょうき}は{早期|そうき}に{治療|ちりょう}すれば{治癒|ちゆ}する{可能性|かのうせい}が{高|たか}い。",
      "english": "If treated early, there is a high possibility of this disease being cured.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A formal medical term that implies complete recovery, not just improvement. The intransitive verb {治癒|ちゆ}する means the condition heals on its own or is healed, while {治療|ちりょう}する (to treat) describes the active process of medical intervention.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {自然|しぜん}{治癒|ちゆ}: natural healing; spontaneous recovery\n- {治癒|ちゆ}{率|りつ}: cure rate\n- {治癒|ちゆ}{力|りょく}: healing power\n- {完全|かんぜん}{治癒|ちゆ}: complete cure\n- {治癒|ちゆ}{不能|ふのう}: incurable\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {治|なお}る: to get better; to heal — the everyday word for recovering from illness or injury\n- {回復|かいふく}する: to recover — broader; includes recovering strength, energy, or normal function, not just curing disease\n- {治療|ちりょう}する: to treat; to cure — the active medical process, while {治癒|ちゆ} describes the result",
